/* =====================================================================
   js/shapes.js - the shapes the 3D object morphs into while you scroll.
   Pre-computed once (the page does no point maths itself): every shape is already a set of dots + lines, and every shape is a real 3D object.
   Order on the page: hero = Earth globe (denser dots on land), then the header icons as inflated 3D objects: services, xp (experience), edu, cert, tools, skills, work (portfolio), contact.
   Keys match the data-blob names in index.html - do not rename them.
   Each shape has two versions: d = desktop (200 dots), m = phone width (60 dots, breakpoint = max-width 899px).
     p = dots as flat x,y,z triples, in thousandths (1000 = the object radius; x right, y up, z towards the viewer)
     e = lines as flat pairs of dot numbers (0-based index into p)
     a = dot numbers that glow in the accent (orange) colour when the section highlights this shape
   Every shape has the SAME number of dots (200 / 60), so each dot simply travels from its place in one shape to its place in the next.
   ===================================================================== */
